the national debt crosses the 20  trillion dollar mark it was big news  when our national debt passed the 20  trillion dollar bond  what's less understood is exactly why  having such a massive debt as a bad  thing the sheer size of the existing  debt is deeply worrying to economist on  both the left and the right to agree  that when debt reaches 90% of GDP it  means painfully slow economic growth  creating what's called a debt overhang a  group of progressive economist  affiliated with the University of  Massachusetts predicted in 2013 that a  debt burden at that level would result  in an annual growth rate of just 2.2  percent which means economic stagnation  and anemic job growth so when will our  debt load cross the 90% threshold it's  actually been at more than 100 percent  of GDP for years now periods of slow  growth associated with that overhangs  almost always lasts more than a decade  and sometimes stretch out over a quarter  century that means that in 25 years the  overall economy will be about 75 percent  the size of would have been if the  government had only gotten the debt in  check countries like New Zealand Canada  and Germany have demonstrated that when  governments reduce debt good things  happen u.s. spending by contrast has  been above 20% of GDP for years which is  well above the historical average  no wonder the Congressional Budget  Office predicts that the economy will  grow less than 2% annually over the next  decade  compare that to growth rates of more  than 3% for much of the post-world War  two period Barack Obama and George W  Bush were leaders who lacked the  integrity to do what's best for the  country by keeping spending and dead in  line President Donald Trump Ossa shows  no interest in explaining to the public  how runaway debt chokes off the future  and that's a failure which we'll all be  paying for for a very long time to come  dead  [Music]  I am the king of debt
 

